@@ -3,3 +3,20 @@
 The Lakeside Windsurf School teaches windsurfing on the lake from April to October, and rents boards and
 sails to its students and to visitors who bring their own experience. This repository holds the software
 of its booking desk, written in TypeScript with no runtime dependency.
+
+`createRentalService()` is exported from `src/index.ts`. Each service keeps its own equipment and
+bookings in memory. Register equipment with `addEquipment({ id, kind, dailyPrice })`, then use
+`quote({ itemId, start, end })` or `book({ itemId, start, end })`. Quotes contain the request fields and
+`total`; bookings also contain a unique `id` within that service.
+
+Prices and totals are nonnegative safe integer euro cents. Equipment IDs must be nonempty and unique;
+`kind` is `board` or `sail`. Periods use explicit UTC ISO-8601 midnight timestamps (for example,
+`2026-06-01T00:00:00Z`), with the end excluded and strictly after the start. Adjacent bookings are
+allowed. Quotes do not reserve equipment or check availability. Invalid inputs and booking conflicts
+throw errors.
+
+Cancellations are not implemented yet. The policy for future cancellation support is no refund when
+cancelled less than 24 hours before the booking starts, and a full refund otherwise (including exactly
+24 hours before the start).
+
+Run `npm test` with Node.js 22.18 or later, which can load the TypeScript source directly.
